We'd like to create a web-based service that can either be used via a fully responsive, web-based front end, or an RESTful API, to generate downloadable QR Codes

All types of QR Code use cases should be included, including (but not limited to)

* Opening a web link (with later integration with our other Go2My.link URL shortner project, to allow for also dynamic links - keeping the QR Code the same, by changing where it links to)
* text
* email
* Phone numbers/calls
* SMS Messages
* Whatsapp Messages/Links
* Zoom Links (based on input Zoom Meeting ID and Passcode/Password OR Zoom Meeting Link)
* 
* geolocation 
* vCard (business card)
* calendar/diary invite/event
* PayPal payment/link
* Bitcoin link/payment
* MP3 file/link
* Video file/link
* PDF File/link
* Image file/link
* App Store links (Apple AppStore/Google Play store)
* Facebook link
* YouTube link
* Wi-Fi Network info (SSID, Network Type and Password)
* LinkedIn link
* etc

The qr code should be generated in various image formats, including (but not limited to:

* JPG
* PNG (with alpha transparency)
* GIf (with alpha transparency)
* SVG (vector)
* WEBP
* JPEG XL
* PDF

The backend should utilise PHP and MYSQL and web standards to create a fully responsive Web UI including a form to input data to generate the QR Code and download the produced code.

The QR Code should also be customizable, by allowing to user to

* change the colour
* QR Code design
* make the background transparent or any other colour
* chose an image to use in the centre (from a predefined set or via a custom uploaded image) - users with a an account to the service can even save some of there own logos that may be reused regularly
* Customisable QR Code shape (most common being square)
* Customisable “corner” elements/shapes
* Customisable frame
* customisable detail/error correction settings (though defaults to standard/recommended settings)
* Other customisable options

It would be great if a user of the web UI could create a account (that will later be integrated with our own SIGNula service). This online account can store the users generated qr code, to allow them to either redownload them later, or modify specific settings or create different variations.

This same account can also be part of a universal “organisation” account to help a company to manage their own company qr codes as part of a “premium” service

All of this should also be possible to use a RESTful API to generate or download QR codes. In fact the web based frontend could just be an implantation of one that calls on this API

The web based Ui must be fully responsive, and adapt to various screen sizes, orientations and screen DPI configurations. Support for High density and HDR displays should also be considered, along side dark or “light” modes.



========================
*TECH STACK and specific instructions*
========================
Please use the following technologies for development of the entire 'Portal' project
* PHP (minimum PHP 8.5 for longevity - current as of November 2025 - but with backward compatibility for PHP 8.4 as well (via conditional statements etc) where necessary.
	* PHP code should
		* Use PHP Predefined Constants wherever possible to aid with host platform neutrality (ie, use DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR instead of '/' in paths, PHP_EOL etc)
		* Full notation for code blocks such as (but not limited to) IF statements, no shortened notation
		* source code should be indented appropriately (upon deployment, code CAN be minified to conserve bandiwidth, but from a dev point everything MUST be easy to read and follow, so indentation is extremely important) with detailed inline comments/annotations to assith with code readibility, understanding, debugging and future learning/maintenance of code
			* Comments can/should provide links to external (preferrably official) documentation for further guidance. 
		* A modular development structure
		* Minimise code duplication but grouping shared code and reusing/reaccessing them via PHP REQUIRE, REQUIRE_ONCE, INCLUDE & INCLUDE_ONCE
		
		  appropriate checks and error handling for REQUIRED and INCLUDED components should be done to avoid errors should files not exist/not be retrievable
		* Provide "switches" (perhaps via URL Parameters or other means) to enable detailed PHP error visiblity by use of a URL Param such as &debug=true (for dev purposes only)
		* log PHP errors/notifictions/warnings (including severity, PHP error code, PHP Error title, error detail, backtrace) to a table in the backend database along with any other errors from components and requested page URL and request headers to assist with debugging/trouble shooting.
		* Log general application activity (not just errors/notifications/warnings/problems) to assist with future development and prooduct support

* MySQL Backend Database (connectin
	* Interactions between PHP & MySQL via MySQLi only
	* Use Prepared Statements for all SQL run in PHP - this is to help manage often re-used types of queries and also help with embedded code/query security mechanism to minimise SQL code enjection exploits(?) 
	* Backend database to be used for ALL settings and config as well as records pertaining the Short Links (and integration with a separate QRCode generator app)
	* Settings should also be stored in the database, including credentials (keys, secrets etc) for third-party services/libraries (like MS365 etc)
	* any confidential secrets/keys (labelled as "isSensitive") must be SALTed and cryptographically encrypted using the latest industry standards for such functionality and sensitive information, before entry into the database to ensure data security. Encryption of these confidential info should also use SALT for added security. When retrieving these fields, they should also be decrypted for use.

* HTML5
	* Must be fully HTML5 compliant, and using modern HTML5 elements, standards and methodologies
    * generated web pages should ALL be fully responsive, and dynamically adjust to the device it is being used on (large screen monitor/smart tv, tabel, phone etc) and at various DPI resolutions and orientations.
    * Happy to use third-party libraries to facilitate this, including bootstrap, and graphics/icons tools like FontAwesome
        For third-party libraries, please use the latest versions and refer to them via their official CDN repositories in the first instance. We're however also happy to have some local copies but these shouold be a contingency more than anything else.

* For bot protection of shortlink creation (main website A) form submission (support for both, in order of preference, but the service used depends on provision of required API Keys/secrets)
	* CloudFlare Turnstile
	* ReCapture
	

========================	
*SPECIFIC REQUIREMENTS*
========================

------------------------	
*Overall*
------------------------
* While this will be hosted on Dreamhost shared hosting initially, please include flexibility for hosting on other PHP/MySQL supporting platforms, as such please use PHP constants and predefined constants wherever possible for platform neutrality/flexibility.
* Given the project will (at least) initially be hosted on Dreamhost's Shared Hosting platform, access to CLI is not possible, as such access to tools like Composer cannot be relied upon. This means any third-party libraries that need to be installed/self-hosted (and cant just be used via referencing CDNs) need to be specifically called out and hosted on local server.

------------------------	
*User Accounts*
------------------------
* A user can register an Organisation. This would create the Organisation and their individual user account under that organisation. As the persson creating the organisation, they will also be made Global Admin of that organisation.
	* Organisation Global Admins can also setup new users within the Organisation with either Admin privileges (admin, but with fewer 'powers' than Global Admin.) or Regular USer access.
	* Organisation Regular Users can only create new short links. Modifying of existing short links will be a defineable permission.
	* Organisation Global Admins will also be the only account able to manage which domain names are assoicated with the organisation, manager all users, manage subscription/payments etc.
	* Global Admins will also be able to setup Single Sign On using corporate providers such as (but not necessarily limited to):
		* Microsoft 365
		* Google Workspace
		* self-hosted wordpress.
		
		Any SSO account MUST also be linked to a local/internal account within the application.
		Support for linking multiple accounts from these corporate account providers (MS365, Google Workspace etc) should also be possible, but can be fully configured what limitations there are by the Organisational Global Admin
	* Organisational Admins can 'invite' other members to create an account. this should send an email with a tokanised link which would create the user within the organisation
* Local accounts will be used first, but we plan on rolling out integration with our SIGNula, our other first-party service, via API integration when it is ready for release. Once ready, provide a mechanism to link local account(s) to SIGNula (either via linking to existing SIGNula accounts or creating new ones)

------------------------	
*API*
------------------------
Secure API (utilising API Keys/CSRF and other security standard mechanisms) must also be supported, with the following functionality

* Create QR Codes
    Including all customisable features, noted above
* Save QR Codes on online account - account users only
* Manage/tweak existing QR Codes - account users only

API should have the capability to return data in the following formats:
* JSON (default)
    associated JSON schema shouold be defined as well to help with JSON validation-checks
* XML (very structured with embedded XSLT for easier view in browser)

API can also be used to create a companion mobile app or managing your short URLs and user acounts.

As with the main components of the app, we do not want to expose that we use PHP for the backend workings of the API, as such API endpoints should not be link create.php. Instead maybe have the actual API endpoint processing in a index.php within a create subdirectory (for example).

Detailed API documentation should be provided online for using the API, using Swagger/OpenAPI standards

------------------------
	*Directory/File Structure*
------------------------
Within this repository, ALL components that need to be uploaded to the web must be within web/:


<server>
├── _auth_keys/                 	← Site/Server-Wide 🔐 MS365 / DB creds / reCapture / Cloudflare Turnstile & other API Keys (outside web root)
│   ├── auth_creds.php				← Stored securely (not accessible via web)
├── _includes/                  	← Stores Site/Server-wide shared 'includes' that are not directly publically accessible
├── _functions/                		← Stores Site/Server-wide shared 'functions' (PHP or other) that used via php include/require and are not directly publically accessible
├── _libraries/                 	← Stores Site/Server-wide shared 'libraries' (dompdf, Parsedown etc)
├── _uploads/                 		← Stores Site/Server-wide 'uploads' that are not directly publically accessible
├── _backups/                 		← Stores Site/Server-wide 'backups' that are not directly publically accessible
├── CueRCode.net/			← Main Website (A): CueRCode.net - public/PR/"face of the service" website
│   ├── _auth_keys/                 ← Website specific DB creds (outside web root) IF different from side/server wide wide
│   │   ├── auth_creds.php          ← Stored securely (not accessible via web)
│   ├── _includes/                  ← Website specific shared 'includes' that are not directly publically accessible
│   ├── _functions/                 ← Website specific shared 'functions' (PHP or other) that used via php include/require and are not directly publically accessible
│   ├── _libraries/                 ← Website specific shared 'libraries' (dompdf, Parsedown etc)
│   ├── _uploads/                 	← Website specific 'uploads' that are not directly publically accessible
│   ├── _backups/                 	← Website specific 'backups' that are not directly publically accessible
│   ├── private_html/               ← Website Private HTML (placeholder structure element, may never be used)
│   ├── public_html/                ← Website public web root (publicly accessible via web)
│   ├── public_html_dev_alpha/		← Website Beta Development web root (publicly accessible via web, but may have auth restrictions via either .htaccess or other mechanisms)
│   ├── public_html_dev_beta/		← Website Beta Development web root (publicly accessible via web, but may have auth restrictions via either .htaccess or other mechanisms)
